-*   `DELTA`: Constant step size. Value: 0.005 [S3, unofficial].
-*   `volume_scale`: Scaling factor for the unit cube to match volume dimensions [S2, unofficial].
+*   `uMinGrayVal` / `uMaxGrayVal`: Minimum and maximum volume value thresholds. Typical values: 0.001 and 1.0 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `uAbsorptionModeIndex`: Switches between rendering modes (0: Simple accumulation, 1: Standard alpha blending, 2: Max projection) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `volume_scale`: Scaling factor for the unit cube to support non-uniform volume dimensions [S2, unofficial].
 
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Zooming:** Rendering front faces causes clipping when the camera zooms inside the volume, as front faces project behind the camera. Rendering only back faces in Pass 1 and front faces in Pass 2 avoids this [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Tangent Rays:** If the entry point equals the exit point, the ray length is zero. The shader must discard the fragment to avoid division by zero [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Loop Limits:** GLSL compilers may have limits on loop unrolling or iteration counts. Using a large constant (e.g., 4095) with an explicit break condition is often safer than a variable loop bound [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** Using `GL_RGBA16F` for the back-face texture provides sufficient precision for coordinate storage [S4, unofficial].
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Degenerate Rays:** If the entry point equals the exit point (e.g., ray misses the box or is tangent), the ray length is zero. The shader must discard the fragment to avoid division by zero or infinite loops [S4, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Zooming Issues:** Rendering only front faces causes issues when zooming in, as front faces project behind the camera and are clipped, leaving pixels unrendered. Rendering only back faces avoids this [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** The back-face texture uses `GL_RGBA16F` to maintain precision for 3D coordinates [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Loop Termination:** GLSL loops may require a large constant upper bound (e.g., 1600) with an explicit break condition due to compiler limitations [S1, S4, unofficial].
+*   **Boundary Checks:** The loop must break if the current position goes outside the $[0,1]$ range to prevent out-of-bounds texture access [S1, unofficial].
 
